/*! \mainpage Project Documentation

\section intro_sec Introduction
This document provides an overview of the project's architecture, components, and interaction flow. It is intended for developers who need to understand the codebase structure and how different parts of the system work together.

\section arch_overview Architecture Overview

The project follows a modular architecture, with clear separation of concerns between modules, services, routes, and controllers.

\subsection modules Modules
Modules represent independent features or functionalities within the application.  Examples might include `UserModule`, `AuthModule`, or `ProductModule`.

\subsection services Services
Services encapsulate business logic and data access. They are responsible for performing specific tasks and interacting with data sources.

\subsection routes Routes
Routes define the API endpoints and map them to specific controller actions.

\subsection controllers Controllers
Controllers handle incoming requests, orchestrate the execution of services, and return responses to the client.

\section interaction_flow Interaction Flow

The following diagram illustrates the interaction flow between the different components of the system.

\dot
digraph Architecture {
    rankdir=LR;
    node [shape=rectangle];

    subgraph cluster_modules {
        label = "Modules";
        UserModule [label="User Module"];
        AuthModule [label="Auth Module"];
        ProductModule [label="Product Module"];
    }

